<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 23 June, from 1266 to 2016.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/venice" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venice.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1266">1266 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">760 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Venice captures the whole Genoese fleet off Trapani</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Venetian fleet under Jacopo Dondulo captured all 27 ships of the Genoese fleet under Lanfranco Borbonino off Trapani, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-saint-sabas">War of Saint Sabas</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> was fought over control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-saint-sabas">War of Saint Sabas</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1280 CE <span class="tih-ago">746 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Granada defeats Castile and León at the Battle of Moclín</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Troops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> defeated the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León at Moclín, in the battle also called the Disaster of Moclín. Ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasrid-dynasty">Nasrid dynasty</a>, Granada was the last independent Muslim state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1305">1305 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">721 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France and Flanders make peace at Athis-sur-Orge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a> and Robert III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-athis-sur-orge">Treaty of Athis-sur-Orge</a>, ending the Franco-Flemish War after the French victory at Mons-en-Pévèle. It imposed on Flanders a heavy indemnity, acts of penance and the demolition of town fortifications.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-athis-sur-orge">Treaty of Athis-sur-Orge</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1314">1314 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">712 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Bannockburn begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the first day, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a> killed the English knight Henry de Bohun in single combat before the armies. Edward II's larger army was routed the next day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1757">1757 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Clive defeats the Nawab of Bengal at Plassey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Helped by the defection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-jafar">Mir Jafar</a>, Clive's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> troops defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraj-ud-daulah">Siraj ud-Daulah</a>. The victory gave the Company control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and launched British territorial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">June Days uprising erupts in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Workers rose after the government closed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-workshops">National Workshops</a>. General Cavaignac crushed them in four days; thousands were killed and many more deported.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1868">1868 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Latham Sholes patents a typewriter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sholes and his partners received a patent for a 'Type-Writer'. Developed further and sold by Remington, it popularised the QWERTY keyboard and transformed office work.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nixon approves using the CIA to block the Watergate inquiry</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a taped conversation, Nixon agreed that the CIA should ask the FBI to halt its investigation. The release of this 'smoking gun' tape in August 1974 forced his resignation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2016">2016 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">10 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United Kingdom votes to leave the European Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a referendum, 52 per cent voted to leave the EU. Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Cameron resigned, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> formally left in January 2020.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 23 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/caesarion"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/caesarion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Caesarion</span><span class="tp">47–30 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giambattista-vico"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giambattista-vico.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giambattista Vico</span><span class="tp">1668–1744</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/josephine-de-beauharnais"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/josephine-de-beauharnais.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joséphine de Beauharnais</span><span class="tp">1763–1814</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-viii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-viii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward VIII</span><span class="tp">1894–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alan-turing"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alan-turing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alan Turing</span><span class="tp">1912–1954</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/virbhadra-singh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/virbhadra-singh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Virbhadra Singh</span><span class="tp">1934–2021</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martti-ahtisaari"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martti-ahtisaari.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martti Ahtisaari</span><span class="tp">1937–2023</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 23 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-probus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-probus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry IV Probus</span><span class="tp">c. 1258–1290</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-mendoza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-de-mendoza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro de Mendoza</span><span class="tp">c. 1487–1537</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/turgut-reis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/turgut-reis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Turgut Reis</span><span class="tp">c. 1485–1565</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/theophilus-shepstone"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/theophilus-shepstone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Theophilus Shepstone</span><span class="tp">1817–1893</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andreas-papandreou"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andreas-papandreou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andreas Papandreou</span><span class="tp">1919–1996</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
